===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|ugge}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|uggr||fear, apprehension, dread}}, related to {{cog|non|ógn||terror, threat, dispute}} and {{m|non|agi||terror, strife, fear, punishment}}. More at {{l|en|awe}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ugg}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[fear|Fear]]; [[horror]].
# {{lb|en|dialectal}} A [[surfeit]].

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|ugly}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|uggen}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|ugga||to fear}}, see above.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ugg}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|ugg}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[dread]], [[loathe]] or [[disgust]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To fear, be [[horrified]]; [[shudder]] with horror.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To give a [[surfeit]] to.

